-- The built-in exercise library as the catalogue has it: 369 exercises -- 96 dumbbell, 87 barbell, 33 bodyweight, 16 other, 62 cable, 62 machine, 13 kettlebell
-- (94 with an attachment, each attachment that changes the movement its own exercise), each
-- with its guide, its other names to search by, and its setup (equipment, grip, attachment,
-- pulley, how it's loaded).
--
-- Named simply wherever the drawing already shows the detail: "Leg Press", not "45-Degree Leg
-- Press"; "Pec Deck", not "Pec Deck Machine"; "Dumbbell Curl", not "Standing Dumbbell Bicep Curl";
-- a cable exercise that only comes one way without its handle ("Cable Face Pull"). A handle stays in
-- the name where the same movement comes with several (the seated cable rows, the pulldowns).
--
-- Retired (27): Dumbbell Tate Press, Barbell Floor Press, Pendlay Row, Deficit Deadlift, Behind-the-Neck Press, Barbell High Pull, Barbell Static Hold, Barbell Side Bend, Jump Squat, Box Jump, Mountain Climber, Burpee, Band Pull-Apart, Band Face Pull, Resistance Band Row, Resistance Band Chest Press, Suspension Trainer Row, Suspension Trainer Chest Press, Medicine Ball Slam, Wall Ball, Medicine Ball Chest Pass, Battle Rope Waves, Battle Rope Slams, Sled Push, Sled Drag, Swiss Bar Bench Press, Svend Press -- hidden from the library and
-- the picker, never deleted: a workout that logged one keeps it, with its drawing and guide.
--
-- GENERATED by supabase/catalog/generate.mjs from the catalogue in supabase/catalog -- change the
-- catalogue and run `npm run db:catalog`, never this file by hand once it's applied.
--
-- Safe for existing history: a built-in that was already here keeps its row (and so every
-- workout, set and record logged against it), its muscle group, its measurement and its sides.
-- The machine and cable built-ins that were here without a guide are renamed to say their
-- standard setup ("Lat Pulldown" -> "Lat Pulldown — Wide-Grip Straight Bar"), the old name kept
-- as a search alias. Everything else is new rows. Nothing is deleted, merged or moved, and no
-- one's own exercise is touched.

-- The new movement patterns: knee extension and flexion, hip abduction and adduction, shoulder
-- rotation, dips and conditioning.
alter table public.exercises drop constraint exercises_movement_pattern_known;
alter table public.exercises
  add constraint exercises_movement_pattern_known check (
    movement_pattern is null or movement_pattern in ('horizontal_push', 'vertical_push', 'horizontal_pull', 'vertical_pull', 'hinge', 'squat', 'lunge', 'hip_extension', 'fly', 'pullover', 'raise', 'shrug', 'curl', 'triceps_extension', 'wrist', 'calf_raise', 'carry', 'core_flexion', 'core_rotation', 'anti_extension', 'lateral_flexion', 'get_up', 'hold', 'knee_extension', 'knee_flexion', 'hip_abduction', 'hip_adduction', 'shoulder_rotation', 'dip', 'conditioning')
  );

